  "body": "In `TlsIdentity.loadOrCreateKeyStore`, I create a PKCS12 `KeyStore`, generate an RSA key pair and certificate when needed, add them to the store, and persist it. RVSec reported that the observed `KeyStore` call sequence was not one it accepts.\n\nI replaced `setKeyEntry` with `setEntry` using `KeyStore.PrivateKeyEntry` and `KeyStore.PasswordProtection`. The alias, generated private key, certificate chain, password, and subsequent store operation remain unchanged, so the surrounding key generation and persistence flow is preserved.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Bras\u00edlia (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
